{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VgGSECDP3n7bGA1T3hRg8B","type":"tool_result","content":"1\textends Node\n2\t## A6 Effect A (hit spark): starts the four pooled HitSpark emitters that main.tscn parents to Main\n3\t## (CHANGE-BRIEF.md, Effect A, observable rules 1-6). Reads the fight's signals, main.paused and\n4\t## main.hitstop; writes nothing but its own emitters' position, emitting and speed_scale. Every\n5\t## particle setting lives in res://effects/hit_spark.tscn.\n6\t\n7\tconst SLOT_NAMES := [\"HitSpark0\", \"HitSpark1\", \"HitSpark2\", \"HitSpark3\"]\n8\t\n9\tvar main: Node\n10\tvar slots: Array[CPUParticles2D] = []\n11\tvar busy: Array[bool] = []\n12\tvar started: Array[int] = []         # start order of each slot's current burst, for \"oldest\"\n13\tvar _next := 0\n14\t\n15\t\n16\tfunc _ready() -> void:\n17\t\tprocess_physics_priority = 10    # after main (0), so this tick's hitstop is already set\n18\t\tmain = get_parent()\n19\t\tfor i in SLOT_NAMES.size():\n20\t\t\tvar slot := main.get_node(SLOT_NAMES[i]) as CPUParticles2D\n21\t\t\tslots.append(slot)\n22\t\t\tbusy.append(false)\n23\t\t\tstarted.append(-1)\n24\t\tfor f in [main.get_node(\"P1\"), main.get_node(\"P2\")]:\n25\t\t\tf.attack_resolved.connect(_on_attack_resolved)\n26\t\tmain.round_started.connect(_on_round_started)\n27\t\tmain.paused_changed.connect(func(_p): _apply_speed())\n28\t\n29\t\n30\tfunc _physics_process(_delta: float) -> void:\n31\t\t_apply_speed()\n32\t\n33\t\n34\t## Rules 1-3: one burst per \"hit\", at its point, in a free slot; the oldest slot if all four are busy.\n35\tfunc _on_attack_resolved(_f: Node, _kind: String, result: String, point: Vector2) -> void:\n36\t\tif result != \"hit\":\n37\t\t\treturn\n38\t\t# A slot is busy while its one-shot burst is still emitting (4.7.2 turns `emitting` false when\n39\t\t# the lifetime ends). Read from the emitters, not from `finished`: after a round reset each\n40\t\t# slot sends a late `finished` that could mark a new burst free (state test, 2026-11-08).\n41\t\tfor k in slots.size():\n42\t\t\tbusy[k] = slots[k].emitting\n43\t\tvar i := busy.find(false)\n44\t\tif i < 0:\n45\t\t\ti = started.find(started.min())\n46\t\tvar slot := slots[i]\n47\t\tslot.position = point\n48\t\tslot.restart()\n49\t\tbusy[i] = true\n50\t\tstarted[i] = _next\n51\t\t_next += 1\n52\t\n53\t\n54\t## Rule 5: the game's pause and hitstop do not pause the tree, so the emitters are frozen here.\n55\tfunc _apply_speed() -> void:\n56\t\tvar s := 0.0 if (main.paused or main.hitstop > 0) else 1.0\n57\t\tfor slot in slots:\n58\t\t\tslot.speed_scale = s\n59\t\n60\t\n61\t## Rule 6: a new round clears every burst without emitting a new one.\n62\tfunc _on_round_started(_n: int) -> void:\n63\t\tfor i in slots.size():\n64\t\t\tslots[i].restart()\n65\t\t\tslots[i].emitting = false\n66\t\t\tbusy[i] = false\n67\t\t\tstarted[i] = -1\n68\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"448404b5-eb92-49c5-9cad-ea968beeb155","uuid":"9ca1e708-08bb-4070-91ac-6732c2ca1e79","timestamp":"2026-11-08T21:49:06.066Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"D:\\courses\\7270\\walker-dusk-duel-zhaohui-li\\godot\\effects\\hit_spark_pool.gd","content":"extends Node\n## A6 Effect A (hit spark): starts the four pooled HitSpark emitters that main.tscn parents to Main\n## (CHANGE-BRIEF.md, Effect A, observable rules 1-6). Reads the fight's signals, main.paused and\n## main.hitstop; writes nothing but its own emitters' position, emitting and speed_scale. Every\n## particle setting lives in res://effects/hit_spark.tscn.\n\nconst SLOT_NAMES := [\"HitSpark0\", \"HitSpark1\", \"HitSpark2\", \"HitSpark3\"]\n\nvar main: Node\nvar slots: Array[CPUParticles2D] = []\nvar busy: Array[bool] = []\nvar started: Array[int] = []         # start order of each slot's current burst, for \"oldest\"\nvar _next := 0\n\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tprocess_physics_priority = 10    # after main (0), so this tick's hitstop is already set\n\tmain = get_parent()\n\tfor i in SLOT_NAMES.size():\n\t\tvar slot := main.get_node(SLOT_NAMES[i]) as CPUParticles2D\n\t\tslots.append(slot)\n\t\tbusy.append(false)\n\t\tstarted.append(-1)\n\tfor f in [main.get_node(\"P1\"), main.get_node(\"P2\")]:\n\t\tf.attack_resolved.connect(_on_attack_resolved)\n\tmain.round_started.connect(_on_round_started)\n\tmain.paused_changed.connect(func(_p): _apply_speed())\n\n\nfunc _physics_process(_delta: float) -> void:\n\t_apply_speed()\n\n\n## Rules 1-3: one burst per \"hit\", at its point, in a free slot; the oldest slot if all four are busy.\nfunc _on_attack_resolved(_f: Node, _kind: String, result: String, point: Vector2) -> void:\n\tif result != \"hit\":\n\t\treturn\n\t# A slot is busy while its one-shot burst is still emitting (4.7.2 turns `emitting` false when\n\t# the lifetime ends). Read from the emitters, not from `finished`: after a round reset each\n\t# slot sends a late `finished` that could mark a new burst free (state test, 2026-11-08).\n\tfor k in slots.size():\n\t\tbusy[k] = slots[k].emitting\n\tvar i := busy.find(false)\n\tif i < 0:\n\t\ti = started.find(started.min())\n\tvar slot := slots[i]\n\tslot.position = point\n\tslot.restart()\n\tbusy[i] = true\n\tstarted[i] = _next\n\t_next += 1\n\n\n## Rule 5: the game's pause and hitstop do not pause the tree, so the emitters are frozen here.\nfunc _apply_speed() -> void:\n\tvar s := 0.0 if (main.paused or main.hitstop > 0) else 1.0\n\tfor slot in slots:\n\t\tslot.speed_scale = s\n\n\n## Rule 6: a new round clears every burst without emitting a new one.\nfunc _on_round_started(_n: int) -> void:\n\tfor i in slots.size():\n\t\tslots[i].restart()\n\t\tslots[i].emitting = false\n\t\tbusy[i] = false\n\t\tstarted[i] = -1\n","numLines":68,"startLine":1,"totalLines":68}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01VgGSECDP3n7bGA1T3hRg8B","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
