{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016QNJHmVRkNSRF8d6Lahkbi","type":"tool_result","content":"1\textends SceneTree\n2\t## A6 Effect A (hit spark): headless state test of the trigger code (res://effects/hit_spark_pool.gd)\n3\t## against CHANGE-BRIEF.md, Effect A, observable rules 1-6. Run from the repo root, through the wrapper:\n4\t##   scripts/run-test.sh test_hit_spark_state.gd 60\n5\t## As in test_hurt_flash.gd, main's _physics_process stays on: the fight runs in the real loop and P1\n6\t## is driven by key events read by its PlayerController. The pool's trigger is never called.\n7\t## Writes to game state, each printed:\n8\t##   HARNESS  P2's controller is set to null when a round starts (scenarios A, B, C, E, F), so\n9\t##            Aotake stands still; scenario D keeps the game's own CpuController.\n10\t##   SETUP    scenario F calls the game's own main.start_fight_now() mid-burst (rule 6, Zhaohui's\n11\t##            choice (b)), inside a physics tick.\n12\t## What a headless run sees: each emitter's node state (emitting, position, speed_scale, parent) once\n13\t## per physics tick and once per frame, and its 'finished' signal. The dummy renderer draws nothing\n14\t## and CPUParticles2D has no live particle count, so the particles themselves are not seen.\n15\t## A \"fire\" is a slot whose emitting goes false -> true, or whose position changes while it is\n16\t## emitting, from one tick to the next (restart() has no signal of its own). The pool's own arrays\n17\t## are read only to report the all-four-busy fallback; no assertion of a fire depends on them.\n18\t\n19\tconst SLOT_NAMES := [\"HitSpark0\", \"HitSpark1\", \"HitSpark2\", \"HitSpark3\"]\n20\tconst LIFETIME_TICKS := 36               # hit_spark.tscn lifetime 0.6 s x 60 ticks/s\n21\tconst HITSTOP := 4                       # main.gd HITSTOP_FRAMES\n22\tconst HOLD_TICKS := 3                    # how long each key is held down\n23\tconst POS_EPS := 1.0                     # rule 2: within 1 px in Main coordinates\n24\tconst WALL_LIMIT_MS := 100000            # watchdog, under the wrapper's 120 s\n25\t\n26\tvar checks := 0\n27\tvar failures := 0\n28\tvar finished_run := false\n29\tvar main: Node\n30\tvar pool: Node\n31\tvar slots: Array = []\n32\tvar ticklog: TickLog\n33\tvar sampler: Sampler\n34\tvar setup_call: SetupCall\n35\tvar results := []                        # attack_resolved of both fighters\n36\tvar finished_log := []                   # {tick, slot}\n37\tvar round_ticks := []                    # ticks on which round_started was emitted\n38\tvar life_unpaused := -1                  # scenario B: hit tick -> emitting false, in ticks\n39\t\n40\t\n41\t## Records every slot once per physics tick, after main (0), the pool (10) and SetupCall (50).\n42\tclass TickLog extends Node:\n43\t\tvar main: Node\n44\t\tvar slots: Array = []\n45\t\tvar recording := false\n46\t\tvar ticks := {}\n47\t\tvar order := []\n48\t\tvar last_tick := -1\n49\t\tvar prev: Array = []\n50\t\tvar fires := []                      # {tick, slot, pos}\n51\t\n52\t\tfunc _ready() -> void:\n53\t\t\tprocess_physics_priority = 1000\n54\t\n55\t\tfunc reset(m: Node, s: Array) -> void:\n56\t\t\tmain = m\n57\t\t\tslots = s\n58\t\t\tticks.clear()\n59\t\t\torder.clear()\n60\t\t\tfires.clear()\n61\t\t\tprev = []\n62\t\t\tfor i in s.size():\n63\t\t\t\tprev.append([false, Vector2.INF, 1.0])\n64\t\n65\t\tfunc _physics_process(_delta: float) -> void:\n66\t\t\tif not (recording and is_instance_valid(main)):\n67\t\t\t\treturn\n68\t\t\tlast_tick = Engine.get_physics_frames()\n69\t\t\tvar now := []\n70\t\t\tfor i in slots.size():\n71\t\t\t\tvar e: CPUParticles2D = slots[i]\n72\t\t\t\tvar st := [e.emitting, e.position, e.speed_scale]\n73\t\t\t\tif st[0] and (not prev[i][0] or st[1] != prev[i][1]):\n74\t\t\t\t\tfires.append({\"tick\": last_tick, \"slot\": i, \"pos\": st[1]})\n75\t\t\t\tnow.append(st)\n76\t\t\tprev = now\n77\t\t\tticks[last_tick] = {\"slots\": now, \"phase\": main.phase, \"paused\": main.paused,\n78\t\t\t\t\t\"hitstop\": main.hitstop, \"p2\": main.p2.position}\n79\t\t\torder.append(last_tick)\n80\t\n81\t\n82\t## Records speed_scale once per rendered frame, after every other _process.\n83\tclass Sampler extends Node:\n84\t\tvar main: Node\n85\t\tvar slots: Array = []\n86\t\tvar recording := false\n87\t\tvar frames := []                     # [process frame, paused, speeds]\n88\t\tvar started_ms := 0\n89\t\tvar on_watchdog: Callable\n90\t\n91\t\tfunc _ready() -> void:\n92\t\t\tprocess_priority = 1000\n93\t\t\tstarted_ms = Time.get_ticks_msec()\n94\t\n95\t\tfunc _process(_delta: float) -> void:\n96\t\t\tif Time.get_ticks_msec() - started_ms > WALL_LIMIT_MS:\n97\t\t\t\ton_watchdog.call()\n98\t\t\tif recording and is_instance_valid(main):\n99\t\t\t\tframes.append([Engine.get_process_frames(), main.paused,\n100\t\t\t\t\t\tslots.map(func(e): return e.speed_scale)])\n101\t\n102\t\n103\t## Runs one queued SETUP call inside a physics tick, after main and the pool, before TickLog.\n104\tclass SetupCall extends Node:\n105\t\tvar pending: Callable\n106\t\tvar done_tick := -1\n107\t\n108\t\tfunc _ready() -> void:\n109\t\t\tprocess_physics_priority = 50\n110\t\n111\t\tfunc _physics_process(_delta: float) -> void:\n112\t\t\tif pending.is_valid():\n113\t\t\t\tvar fn := pending\n114\t\t\t\tpending = Callable()\n115\t\t\t\tdone_tick = Engine.get_physics_frames()\n116\t\t\t\tfn.call()\n117\t\n118\t\n119\tfunc _initialize() -> void:\n120\t\t_run.call_deferred()\n121\t\n122\t\n123\tfunc _run() -> void:\n124\t\tticklog = TickLog.new()\n125\t\tsampler = Sampler.new()\n126\t\tsampler.on_watchdog = _watchdog\n127\t\tsetup_call = SetupCall.new()\n128\t\troot.add_child(ticklog)\n129\t\troot.add_child(sampler)\n130\t\troot.add_child(setup_call)\n131\t\tfor i in 10:\n132\t\t\tawait process_frame\n133\t\tprint(\"hit spark state test: Godot %s, %d physics ticks/s; headless dummy renderer, nothing is drawn\" % [\n134\t\t\tEngine.get_version_info().string, ProjectSettings.get_setting(\"physics/common/physics_ticks_per_second\")])\n135\t\tcheck(ClassDB.class_has_signal(\"CPUParticles2D\", \"finished\"), \"harness\",\n136\t\t\t\t\"CPUParticles2D has a 'finished' signal in this build (the pool frees slots on it)\")\n137\t\tawait scenario_load()\n138\t\tawait scenario_single_hit()\n139\t\tawait scenario_retrigger()\n140\t\tawait scenario_free_fight()\n141\t\tawait scenario_pause()\n142\t\tawait scenario_round_reset_setup()\n143\t\tfinish()\n144\t\n145\t\n146\t# --- scenarios ---------------------------------------------------------------\n147\t\n148\tfunc scenario_load() -> void:\n149\t\tif not await start_fight(\"A: scene load -> title -> Enter -> intro -> fight, no attack (rules 1, 3, 4)\", false, 30):\n150\t\t\tawait end_fight()\n151\t\t\treturn\n152\t\tvar title_ticks: Array = ticklog.order.filter(func(x): return ticklog.ticks[x][\"phase\"] == \"title\")\n153\t\tvar intro_ticks: Array = ticklog.order.filter(func(x): return ticklog.ticks[x][\"phase\"] == \"intro\")\n154\t\tawait wait_ticks(30)\n155\t\tvar any_on := ticklog.order.any(func(x): return ticklog.ticks[x][\"slots\"].any(func(s): return s[0]))\n156\t\tcheck(ticklog.fires.is_empty() and not any_on and title_ticks.size() >= 30 and intro_ticks.size() >= 50, \"1\",\n157\t\t\t\t\"no slot emitting on any of %d ticks from scene load (%d title, %d intro, then fight), %d fires\" % [\n158\t\t\t\tticklog.order.size(), title_ticks.size(), intro_ticks.size(), ticklog.fires.size()])\n159\t\tvar in_main := slots.size() == 4 and slots.all(func(e): return e is CPUParticles2D and e.get_parent() == main)\n160\t\tvar total := 0\n161\t\tfor e in slots:\n162\t\t\ttotal += e.amount\n163\t\tcheck(in_main and total == 80, \"3, 4\",\n164\t\t\t\t\"4 CPUParticles2D slots, each a child of Main, %d particles in all (brief: 4 x 20 = 80)\" % total)\n165\t\tvar under_fighters := 0\n166\t\tfor f in [main.p1, main.p2]:\n167\t\t\tunder_fighters += f.find_children(\"*\", \"CPUParticles2D\", true, false).size()\n168\t\tcheck(under_fighters == 0, \"4\", \"no particle emitter under P1 or P2 (%d found)\" % under_fighters)\n169\t\tawait end_fight()\n170\t\n171\t\n172\tfunc scenario_single_hit() -> void:\n173\t\tif not await start_fight(\"B: one punch on a standing Aotake (input only) (rules 1, 2, 4, 5)\", false):\n174\t\t\tawait end_fight()\n175\t\t\treturn\n176\t\tif not await walk_into_punch_range():\n177\t\t\tawait end_fight()\n178\t\t\treturn\n179\t\tawait tap(KEY_J, \"J (punch)\")\n180\t\tawait wait_until(func(): return hits().size() >= 1, 30)\n181\t\tvar h := hit(0)\n182\t\tcheck(not h.is_empty(), \"harness\", \"P1's punch from the J key hit P2 (%s)\" % [result_names()])\n183\t\tif h.is_empty():\n184\t\t\tawait end_fight()\n185\t\t\treturn\n186\t\tawait wait_ticks(LIFETIME_TICKS + HITSTOP + 10)\n187\t\tvar t: int = h[\"tick\"]\n188\t\tvar f := fires_on(t)\n189\t\tcheck(f.size() == 1 and ticklog.fires.size() == 1, \"1\",\n190\t\t\t\t\"exactly one slot fired, on the hit tick T = %d (slot %s), and no fire on any other tick (%d in all)\" % [\n191\t\t\t\tt, f.map(func(x): return x[\"slot\"]), ticklog.fires.size()])\n192\t\tif f.size() != 1:\n193\t\t\tawait end_fight()\n194\t\t\treturn\n195\t\tvar i: int = f[0][\"slot\"]\n196\t\tvar e: CPUParticles2D = slots[i]\n197\t\tcheck(e.position.distance_to(h[\"point\"]) <= POS_EPS and e.global_position.distance_to(main.to_global(h[\"point\"])) <= POS_EPS,\n198\t\t\t\t\"2\", \"slot %d at %s, hit point %s (Main coordinates; global %s)\" % [i, e.position, h[\"point\"], e.global_position])\n199\t\tvar fall := fall_after(i, t)\n200\t\tvar moved: float = (tk(fall - 1).get(\"p2\", Vector2.ZERO) as Vector2).distance_to(tk(t).get(\"p2\", Vector2.ZERO))\n201\t\tvar still := true\n202\t\tfor x in range(t, fall):\n203\t\t\tstill = still and tk(x)[\"slots\"][i][1] == h[\"point\"]\n204\t\tcheck(fall > t and still and moved > 3.0, \"4\",\n205\t\t\t\t\"the slot stayed at the hit point for its whole burst (T..T+%d) while P2 was pushed %.1f px\" % [fall - t - 1, moved])\n206\t\tlife_unpaused = fall - t\n207\t\tcheck(fall > t and life_unpaused >= LIFETIME_TICKS + HITSTOP - 1 and life_unpaused <= LIFETIME_TICKS + HITSTOP + 1, \"5\",\n208\t\t\t\t\"emitting went false %d ticks after the hit: 36-tick lifetime + %d hitstop ticks held at speed_scale 0 (want 39-41)\" % [\n209\t\t\t\tlife_unpaused, HITSTOP])\n210\t\tprint(\"    'finished' after this burst on ticks %s (slot %d)\" % [finished_log.map(func(x): return x[\"tick\"] - t), i])\n211\t\tawait end_fight()\n212\t\n213\t\n214\tfunc scenario_retrigger() -> void:\n215\t\tif not await start_fight(\"C: two punches inside one lifetime, Aotake cornered (input only) (rule 3)\", false):\n216\t\t\tawait end_fight()\n217\t\t\treturn\n218\t\tsend_key(KEY_D, true)\n219\t\tprint(\"    INPUT: D (walk right) held from after tick %d, pushing Aotake to the right wall\" % ticklog.last_tick)\n220\t\tvar ok: bool = await wait_until(func(): return main.p2.position.x >= Fighter.ARENA_RIGHT - 0.01, 900)\n221\t\tsend_key(KEY_D, false)\n222\t\tvar idle: bool = await wait_until(func(): return main.p1.state == \"idle\", 30)\n223\t\tcheck(ok and idle, \"harness\", \"Aotake at the right wall (x %.1f), P1 stopped at x %.1f\" % [main.p2.position.x, main.p1.position.x])\n224\t\tawait tap(KEY_J, \"J (punch 1)\")\n225\t\tawait wait_until(func(): return hits().size() >= 1, 30)\n226\t\tawait wait_until(func(): return main.p1.state == \"idle\", 60)\n227\t\tawait tap(KEY_J, \"J (punch 2)\")\n228\t\tawait wait_until(func(): return hits().size() >= 2, 30)\n229\t\tawait wait_ticks(LIFETIME_TICKS * 2 + 2 * HITSTOP + 10)\n230\t\tcheck(hits().size() == 2, \"harness\", \"both punches hit (%s)\" % [result_names()])\n231\t\tif hits().size() != 2:\n232\t\t\tawait end_fight()\n233\t\t\treturn\n234\t\tvar t1: int = hit(0)[\"tick\"]\n235\t\tvar t2: int = hit(1)[\"tick\"]\n236\t\tvar f1 := fires_on(t1)\n237\t\tvar f2 := fires_on(t2)\n238\t\tcheck(t2 - t1 < LIFETIME_TICKS, \"harness\", \"second hit %d ticks after the first, inside one 36-tick lifetime\" % [t2 - t1])\n239\t\tif f1.size() != 1 or f2.size() != 1:\n240\t\t\tcheck(false, \"3\", \"one fire on each hit tick (got %d and %d)\" % [f1.size(), f2.size()])\n241\t\t\tawait end_fight()\n242\t\t\treturn\n243\t\tvar a: int = f1[0][\"slot\"]\n244\t\tvar b: int = f2[0][\"slot\"]\n245\t\tprint(\"    hit 1 tick %d -> slot %d at %s; hit 2 tick %d -> slot %d at %s\" % [t1, a, f1[0][\"pos\"], t2, b, f2[0][\"pos\"]])\n246\t\tcheck(a != b, \"3\", \"the second hit used another slot (%d, then %d), not the active one\" % [a, b])\n247\t\tvar kept := true\n248\t\tfor x in range(t1, t2 + 1):\n249\t\t\tkept = kept and tk(x)[\"slots\"][a][0] and tk(x)[\"slots\"][a][1] == f1[0][\"pos\"]\n250\t\tcheck(kept and tk(t2)[\"slots\"][b][0], \"3\",\n251\t\t\t\t\"slot %d emitted on every tick T1..T2 at its own point, and on T2 both slots are emitting\" % a)\n252\t\tvar fall_a := fall_after(a, t1)\n253\t\tvar fall_b := fall_after(b, t2)\n254\t\tcheck(fall_a > t2 and fall_a < t2 + LIFETIME_TICKS and fall_a < fall_b, \"3\",\n255\t\t\t\t\"slot %d ran its own burst to the end: emitting false at T1+%d = T2+%d, before slot %d at T2+%d (a restart would end after T2+36)\" % [\n256\t\t\t\ta, fall_a - t1, fall_a - t2, b, fall_b - t2])\n257\t\tawait end_fight()\n258\t\n259\t\n260\tfunc scenario_free_fight() -> void:\n261\t\tif not await start_fight(\"D: a whole round against the game's CpuController, then Enter (rules 1, 2, 3, 6 real path)\", true):\n262\t\t\tawait end_fight()\n263\t\t\treturn\n264\t\tawait tap(KEY_J, \"J (punch from across the arena, a whiff)\")\n265\t\tawait wait_ticks(20)\n266\t\tsend_key(KEY_L, true)\n267\t\tprint(\"    INPUT: L (block) held from after tick %d\" % ticklog.last_tick)\n268\t\tawait wait_ticks(200)\n269\t\tsend_key(KEY_L, false)\n270\t\tsend_key(KEY_D, true)\n271\t\tprint(\"    INPUT: D held and J tapped every 24 ticks from after tick %d, until a K.O.\" % ticklog.last_tick)\n272\t\tvar limit := Engine.get_physics_frames() + 4000\n273\t\twhile main.phase == \"fight\" and Engine.get_physics_frames() < limit:\n274\t\t\tsend_key(KEY_J, true)\n275\t\t\tawait wait_ticks(HOLD_TICKS)\n276\t\t\tsend_key(KEY_J, false)\n277\t\t\tawait wait_ticks(21)\n278\t\tsend_key(KEY_D, false)\n279\t\tcheck(main.phase == \"ko\" or main.phase == \"result\", \"harness\", \"the round ended in a K.O. (phase %s)\" % main.phase)\n280\t\tawait wait_until(func(): return main.phase == \"result\", 120)\n281\t\tvar by := {}\n282\t\tfor r in results:\n283\t\t\tvar k := \"%s %s\" % [r[\"who\"], r[\"result\"]]\n284\t\t\tby[k] = by.get(k, 0) + 1\n285\t\tprint(\"    results: %s\" % [by])\n286\t\tcheck(by.get(\"P1 hit\", 0) > 0 and by.get(\"P2 hit\", 0) > 0 and (by.get(\"P1 blocked\", 0) + by.get(\"P2 blocked\", 0)) > 0\n287\t\t\t\tand (by.get(\"P1 whiff\", 0) + by.get(\"P2 whiff\", 0)) > 0, \"harness\",\n288\t\t\t\t\"the round produced hits by both fighters, blocks and whiffs\")\n289\t\tvar n_rounds := round_ticks.size()\n290\t\tawait tap(KEY_ENTER, \"Enter (rematch on the result screen)\")\n291\t\tawait wait_until(func(): return round_ticks.size() > n_rounds, 30)\n292\t\tawait wait_ticks(40)\n293\t\tif round_ticks.size() > n_rounds:\n294\t\t\tvar rs: int = round_ticks[-1]\n295\t\t\tvar off: bool = not tk(rs).get(\"slots\", [[true]]).any(func(s): return s[0])\n296\t\t\tvar later: Array = ticklog.fires.filter(func(x): return x[\"tick\"] >= rs)\n297\t\t\tvar last_fire: int = ticklog.fires[-1][\"tick\"] if not ticklog.fires.is_empty() else -1\n298\t\t\tcheck(off and later.is_empty(), \"6\",\n299\t\t\t\t\t\"real path: on the round_started tick (%d) no slot is emitting and none fires in the next 40 ticks (last burst fired %d ticks earlier, so this path cannot show a live burst being cleared)\" % [\n300\t\t\t\t\trs, rs - last_fire])\n301\t\telse:\n302\t\t\tcheck(false, \"6\", \"Enter on the result screen started a new round\")\n303\t\tawait end_fight()\n304\t\n305\t\n306\tfunc scenario_pause() -> void:\n307\t\tif not await start_fight(\"E: P pressed mid-burst for 40 ticks, then P again (input only) (rule 5)\", false):\n308\t\t\tawait end_fight()\n309\t\t\treturn\n310\t\tif not await walk_into_punch_range():\n311\t\t\tawait end_fight()\n312\t\t\treturn\n313\t\tawait tap(KEY_J, \"J (punch)\")\n314\t\tawait wait_until(func(): return hits().size() >= 1, 30)\n315\t\tawait wait_ticks(HITSTOP + 6)\n316\t\tawait tap(KEY_P, \"P (pause)\")\n317\t\tawait wait_ticks(40)\n318\t\tawait tap(KEY_P, \"P (resume)\")\n319\t\tawait wait_ticks(LIFETIME_TICKS + 10)\n320\t\tvar h := hit(0)\n321\t\tif h.is_empty() or fires_on(h[\"tick\"]).size() != 1:\n322\t\t\tcheck(false, \"harness\", \"the punch hit and one slot fired (%s)\" % [result_names()])\n323\t\t\tawait end_fight()\n324\t\t\treturn\n325\t\tvar t: int = h[\"tick\"]\n326\t\tvar i: int = fires_on(t)[0][\"slot\"]\n327\t\tvar paused: Array = ticklog.order.filter(func(x): return ticklog.ticks[x][\"paused\"])\n328\t\tvar frozen := paused.all(func(x): return ticklog.ticks[x][\"slots\"].all(func(s): return s[2] == 0.0))\n329\t\tvar pf: Array = sampler.frames.filter(func(s): return s[1])\n330\t\tvar frozen_f := pf.all(func(s): return s[2].all(func(v): return v == 0.0))\n331\t\tcheck(paused.size() >= 40 and frozen and pf.size() >= 40 and frozen_f, \"5\",\n332\t\t\t\t\"speed_scale 0 on all 4 slots on all %d paused ticks and %d paused frames\" % [paused.size(), pf.size()])\n333\t\tvar fall := fall_after(i, t)\n334\t\tvar during: bool = paused.all(func(x): return x < fall and ticklog.ticks[x][\"slots\"][i][0])\n335\t\tvar life := fall - t\n336\t\tcheck(during and life_unpaused > 0 and absi(life - life_unpaused - paused.size()) <= 1, \"5\",\n337\t\t\t\t\"the burst's clock stopped while paused: emitting false %d ticks after the hit = %d unpaused (scenario B) + %d paused\" % [\n338\t\t\t\tlife, life_unpaused, paused.size()])\n339\t\tawait end_fight()\n340\t\n341\t\n342\tfunc scenario_round_reset_setup() -> void:\n343\t\tif not await start_fight(\"F: SETUP main.start_fight_now() mid-burst, then a new punch (rule 6, Zhaohui's choice (b))\", false):\n344\t\t\tawait end_fight()\n345\t\t\treturn\n346\t\tif not await walk_into_punch_range():\n347\t\t\tawait end_fight()\n348\t\t\treturn\n349\t\tawait tap(KEY_J, \"J (punch 1)\")\n350\t\tawait wait_until(func(): return hits().size() >= 1, 30)\n351\t\tawait wait_ticks(HITSTOP + 6)\n352\t\tvar h := hit(0)\n353\t\tif h.is_empty() or fires_on(h[\"tick\"]).size() != 1:\n354\t\t\tcheck(false, \"harness\", \"punch 1 hit and one slot fired (%s)\" % [result_names()])\n355\t\t\tawait end_fight()\n356\t\t\treturn\n357\t\tvar i: int = fires_on(h[\"tick\"])[0][\"slot\"]\n358\t\tcheck(tk(ticklog.last_tick)[\"slots\"][i][0], \"harness\", \"slot %d is mid-burst (hit tick +%d)\" % [i, ticklog.last_tick - h[\"tick\"]])\n359\t\tvar fin_before := finished_log.size()\n360\t\tsetup_call.done_tick = -1\n361\t\tsetup_call.pending = func():\n362\t\t\tprint(\"    SETUP (not input): main.start_fight_now() on tick T+%d, slot %d emitting\" % [\n363\t\t\t\tEngine.get_physics_frames() - h[\"tick\"], i])\n364\t\t\tmain.start_fight_now()\n365\t\tawait wait_until(func(): return setup_call.done_tick >= 0, 10)\n366\t\tvar s: int = setup_call.done_tick\n367\t\tawait wait_ticks(LIFETIME_TICKS + 10)\n368\t\tvar off: bool = not tk(s).get(\"slots\", [[true]]).any(func(x): return x[0])\n369\t\tvar quiet: Array = ticklog.fires.filter(func(x): return x[\"tick\"] > h[\"tick\"])\n370\t\tcheck(s >= 0 and off and quiet.is_empty(), \"6\",\n371\t\t\t\t\"on the SETUP tick every slot stopped emitting (slot %d was mid-burst), and no slot fired in the next %d ticks\" % [\n372\t\t\t\ti, LIFETIME_TICKS + 10])\n373\t\tprint(\"    'finished' after the SETUP on ticks %s (slot: ticks after SETUP)\" % [\n374\t\t\tfinished_log.slice(fin_before).map(func(x): return \"%d: %d\" % [x[\"slot\"], x[\"tick\"] - s])])\n375\t\tif not await walk_into_punch_range():\n376\t\t\tawait end_fight()\n377\t\t\treturn\n378\t\tawait tap(KEY_J, \"J (punch 2, in the new round)\")\n379\t\tawait wait_until(func(): return hits().size() >= 2, 30)\n380\t\tawait wait_ticks(5)\n381\t\tvar h2 := hit(1)\n382\t\tvar f2: Array = fires_on(h2[\"tick\"]) if not h2.is_empty() else []\n383\t\tcheck(f2.size() == 1 and (f2[0][\"pos\"] as Vector2).distance_to(h2[\"point\"]) <= POS_EPS, \"6\",\n384\t\t\t\t\"after the reset the next hit fires one slot (%s) at its point\" % [f2.map(func(x): return \"slot %d at %s\" % [x[\"slot\"], x[\"pos\"]])])\n385\t\tawait end_fight()\n386\t\n387\t\n388\t# --- checks over every scenario ---------------------------------------------\n389\t\n390\t## Rules 1 and 2 over the whole scene: on every tick, fires == \"hit\" results of both fighters, each\n391\t## at its point; rule 3's fallback reported if it happened; rule 5 on every tick and frame.\n392\tfunc check_scene() -> void:\n393\t\tvar hit_by := {}\n394\t\tfor r in results:\n395\t\t\tif r[\"result\"] == \"hit\":\n396\t\t\t\thit_by.get_or_add(r[\"tick\"], []).append(r)\n397\t\tvar fire_by := {}\n398\t\tfor f in ticklog.fires:\n399\t\t\tfire_by.get_or_add(f[\"tick\"], []).append(f)\n400\t\tvar bad := []\n401\t\tvar fallback := 0\n402\t\tfor t in hit_by:\n403\t\t\tvar fs: Array = fire_by.get(t, []).duplicate()\n404\t\t\tif fs.size() != hit_by[t].size():\n405\t\t\t\tbad.append(\"tick %d: %d hits, %d fires\" % [t, hit_by[t].size(), fs.size()])\n406\t\t\t\tcontinue\n407\t\t\tfor r in hit_by[t]:\n408\t\t\t\tvar j := -1\n409\t\t\t\tfor k in fs.size():\n410\t\t\t\t\tif (fs[k][\"pos\"] as Vector2).distance_to(r[\"point\"]) <= POS_EPS:\n411\t\t\t\t\t\tj = k\n412\t\t\t\tif j < 0:\n413\t\t\t\t\tbad.append(\"tick %d: no fire at %s\" % [t, r[\"point\"]])\n414\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n415\t\t\t\tif not (r[\"busy\"] as Array).has(false):\n416\t\t\t\t\tfallback += 1\n417\t\t\t\t\tvar oldest: int = r[\"started\"].find(r[\"started\"].min())\n418\t\t\t\t\tif fs[j][\"slot\"] != oldest:\n419\t\t\t\t\t\tbad.append(\"tick %d: all busy, fired slot %d, oldest %d\" % [t, fs[j][\"slot\"], oldest])\n420\t\t\t\tfs.remove_at(j)\n421\t\tfor t in fire_by:\n422\t\t\tif not hit_by.has(t):\n423\t\t\t\tbad.append(\"tick %d: fire with no hit\" % t)\n424\t\tvar other := results.filter(func(r): return r[\"result\"] != \"hit\").size()\n425\t\tcheck(bad.is_empty(), \"1, 2\",\n426\t\t\t\t\"scene: %d fires for %d hits, one per hit on its tick within 1 px of its point; none on %d other results or any other tick%s\" % [\n427\t\t\t\tticklog.fires.size(), hit_by.values().reduce(func(n, a): return n + a.size(), 0), other,\n428\t\t\t\t\"\" if bad.is_empty() else \": \" + \", \".join(bad.slice(0, 5))])\n429\t\tprint(\"    rule 3 fallback (all four slots busy at a hit): %d time(s)%s\" % [fallback,\n430\t\t\t\"\" if fallback else \"; not exercised in this scene\"])\n431\t\tvar wrong := []\n432\t\tfor t in ticklog.order:\n433\t\t\tvar r: Dictionary = ticklog.ticks[t]\n434\t\t\tvar want := 0.0 if (r[\"paused\"] or r[\"hitstop\"] > 0) else 1.0\n435\t\t\tif not r[\"slots\"].all(func(s): return s[2] == want):\n436\t\t\t\twrong.append(t)\n437\t\tvar held: int = ticklog.order.filter(func(t): return ticklog.ticks[t][\"hitstop\"] > 0).size()\n438\t\tcheck(wrong.is_empty(), \"5\",\n439\t\t\t\t\"scene: speed_scale 0 on all 4 slots on every tick with main.paused or main.hitstop > 0 (%d hitstop ticks), 1 on the other %d ticks%s\" % [\n440\t\t\t\theld, ticklog.order.size() - held, \"\" if wrong.is_empty() else \": wrong on ticks %s\" % [wrong.slice(0, 5)]])\n441\t\n442\t\n443\t# --- helpers -----------------------------------------------------------------\n444\t\n445\tfunc start_fight(title: String, cpu: bool, title_ticks := 0) -> bool:\n446\t\tprint(\"\\n== %s ==\" % title)\n447\t\tmain = load(\"res://game/main.tscn\").instantiate()\n448\t\tpool = main.get_node(\"HitSparkPool\")\n449\t\tslots = SLOT_NAMES.map(func(n): return main.get_node(n))\n450\t\tresults.clear()\n451\t\tfinished_log.clear()\n452\t\tround_ticks.clear()\n453\t\tsampler.frames.clear()\n454\t\tticklog.reset(main, slots)\n455\t\tsampler.main = main\n456\t\tsampler.slots = slots\n457\t\t# Connected before main enters the tree, so these run before the pool's handler (snapshot of\n458\t\t# the pool's busy state for the fallback report) and before main's.\n459\t\tfor f in [main.get_node(\"P1\"), main.get_node(\"P2\")]:\n460\t\t\tf.attack_resolved.connect(func(_f, kind, result, point):\n461\t\t\t\tresults.append({\"tick\": Engine.get_physics_frames(), \"who\": \"P1\" if f.name == \"P1\" else \"P2\",\n462\t\t\t\t\t\"kind\": kind, \"result\": result, \"point\": point,\n463\t\t\t\t\t\"busy\": pool.busy.duplicate(), \"started\": pool.started.duplicate()}))\n464\t\tfor i in slots.size():\n465\t\t\tslots[i].finished.connect(func(): finished_log.append({\"tick\": Engine.get_physics_frames(), \"slot\": i}))\n466\t\tmain.round_started.connect(func(_n): round_ticks.append(Engine.get_physics_frames()))\n467\t\tif not cpu:\n468\t\t\tmain.round_started.connect(func(_n): main.p2.controller = null)\n469\t\tticklog.recording = true\n470\t\tsampler.recording = true\n471\t\troot.add_child(main)\n472\t\tawait process_frame\n473\t\tcheck(main.is_physics_processing() and main.p1.controller is PlayerController, \"harness\",\n474\t\t\t\t\"main's _physics_process is on and P1 is driven by its PlayerController\")\n475\t\tawait wait_ticks(title_ticks)\n476\t\tawait tap(KEY_ENTER, \"Enter (title)\")\n477\t\tvar ok := await wait_until(func(): return main.phase == \"fight\", 120)\n478\t\tcheck(ok, \"harness\", \"Enter on the title started round 1; the intro ran into the fight (phase %s)\" % main.phase)\n479\t\tif not cpu:\n480\t\t\tprint(\"    HARNESS (writes no fight state): P2's controller set to null when the round starts, so Aotake stands still\")\n481\t\treturn ok\n482\t\n483\t\n484\tfunc end_fight() -> void:\n485\t\tfor k in [KEY_D, KEY_J, KEY_L, KEY_P, KEY_ENTER]:\n486\t\t\tsend_key(k, false)\n487\t\tsetup_call.pending = Callable()\n488\t\tticklog.recording = false\n489\t\tsampler.recording = false\n490\t\tif is_instance_valid(main):\n491\t\t\tcheck_scene()\n492\t\t\tvar kept := slots.duplicate()\n493\t\t\tmain.queue_free()\n494\t\t\tawait process_frame\n495\t\t\tawait process_frame\n496\t\t\tcheck(kept.all(func(e): return not is_instance_valid(e)), \"4\",\n497\t\t\t\t\t\"freeing Main freed all 4 slots with it\")\n498\t\n499\t\n500\tfunc walk_into_punch_range() -> bool:\n501\t\tvar gap: float = main.p1.reach(\"punch\") + main.p2.body_half_width() - 8.0\n502\t\tsend_key(KEY_D, true)\n503\t\tprint(\"    INPUT: D (walk right) held from after tick %d\" % ticklog.last_tick)\n504\t\tvar ok: bool = await wait_until(func(): return main.p2.position.x - main.p1.position.x <= gap, 300)\n505\t\tsend_key(KEY_D, false)\n506\t\tvar idle: bool = await wait_until(func(): return main.p1.state == \"idle\", 30)\n507\t\tcheck(ok and idle, \"harness\", \"P1 walked to punch range with the D key (gap %.1f px, target <= %.1f) and stopped\" % [\n508\t\t\tmain.p2.position.x - main.p1.position.x, gap])\n509\t\treturn ok and idle\n510\t\n511\t\n512\tfunc hits() -> Array:\n513\t\treturn results.filter(func(r): return r[\"result\"] == \"hit\")\n514\t\n515\t\n516\tfunc hit(index: int) -> Dictionary:\n517\t\tvar h := hits()\n518\t\treturn h[index] if h.size() > index else {}\n519\t\n520\t\n521\tfunc result_names() -> Array:\n522\t\treturn results.map(func(r): return \"%s %s %s\" % [r[\"who\"], r[\"kind\"], r[\"result\"]])\n523\t\n524\t\n525\tfunc fires_on(t: int) -> Array:\n526\t\treturn ticklog.fires.filter(func(f): return f[\"tick\"] == t)\n527\t\n528\t\n529\t## First recorded tick after t0 on which slot i is not emitting, or -1.\n530\tfunc fall_after(i: int, t0: int) -> int:\n531\t\tfor t in ticklog.order:\n532\t\t\tif t > t0 and not ticklog.ticks[t][\"slots\"][i][0]:\n533\t\t\t\treturn t\n534\t\treturn -1\n535\t\n536\t\n537\tfunc tk(t: int) -> Dictionary:\n538\t\treturn ticklog.ticks.get(t, {})\n539\t\n540\t\n541\tfunc send_key(code: Key, pressed: bool) -> void:\n542\t\tvar ev := InputEventKey.new()\n543\t\tev.keycode = code\n544\t\tev.physical_keycode = code\n545\t\tev.pressed = pressed\n546\t\tInput.parse_input_event(ev)\n547\t\n548\t\n549\tfunc tap(code: Key, label: String) -> void:\n550\t\tsend_key(code, true)\n551\t\tprint(\"    INPUT: %s pressed after tick %d\" % [label, ticklog.last_tick])\n552\t\tawait wait_ticks(HOLD_TICKS)\n553\t\tsend_key(code, false)\n554\t\tawait process_frame\n555\t\n556\t\n557\tfunc wait_until(cond: Callable, max_ticks: int) -> bool:\n558\t\tvar limit := Engine.get_physics_frames() + max_ticks\n559\t\twhile not cond.call():\n560\t\t\tif Engine.get_physics_frames() > limit:\n561\t\t\t\treturn false\n562\t\t\tawait process_frame\n563\t\treturn true\n564\t\n565\t\n566\tfunc wait_ticks(n: int) -> void:\n567\t\tvar limit := Engine.get_physics_frames() + n\n568\t\twhile Engine.get_physics_frames() < limit:\n569\t\t\tawait process_frame\n570\t\n571\t\n572\tfunc check(cond: bool, rule: String, msg: String) -> void:\n573\t\tchecks += 1\n574\t\tif not cond:\n575\t\t\tfailures += 1\n576\t\tprint(\"%s [%s] %s\" % [\"PASS\" if cond else \"FAIL\", rule, msg])\n577\t\n578\t\n579\tfunc _watchdog() -> void:\n580\t\tif finished_run:\n581\t\t\treturn\n582\t\tcheck(false, \"harness\", \"watchdog: not finished after %d s of wall-clock time\" % (WALL_LIMIT_MS / 1000))\n583\t\tfinish()\n584\t\n585\t\n586\tfunc finish() -> void:\n587\t\tif finished_run:\n588\t\t\treturn\n589\t\tfinished_run = true\n590\t\tprint(\"%d checks, %d failed\" % [checks, failures])\n591\t\tquit(1 if failures else 0)\n592\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"448404b5-eb92-49c5-9cad-ea968beeb155","uuid":"3085321d-f364-4d2d-8375-cb97403399cd","timestamp":"2026-11-08T21:49:06.614Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"D:\\courses\\7270\\walker-dusk-duel-zhaohui-li\\godot\\tests\\test_hit_spark_state.gd","content":"extends SceneTree\n## A6 Effect A (hit spark): headless state test of the trigger code (res://effects/hit_spark_pool.gd)\n## against CHANGE-BRIEF.md, Effect A, observable rules 1-6. Run from the repo root, through the wrapper:\n##   scripts/run-test.sh test_hit_spark_state.gd 60\n## As in test_hurt_flash.gd, main's _physics_process stays on: the fight runs in the real loop and P1\n## is driven by key events read by its PlayerController. The pool's trigger is never called.\n## Writes to game state, each printed:\n##   HARNESS  P2's controller is set to null when a round starts (scenarios A, B, C, E, F), so\n##            Aotake stands still; scenario D keeps the game's own CpuController.\n##   SETUP    scenario F calls the game's own main.start_fight_now() mid-burst (rule 6, Zhaohui's\n##            choice (b)), inside a physics tick.\n## What a headless run sees: each emitter's node state (emitting, position, speed_scale, parent) once\n## per physics tick and once per frame, and its 'finished' signal. The dummy renderer draws nothing\n## and CPUParticles2D has no live particle count, so the particles themselves are not seen.\n## A \"fire\" is a slot whose emitting goes false -> true, or whose position changes while it is\n## emitting, from one tick to the next (restart() has no signal of its own). The pool's own arrays\n## are read only to report the all-four-busy fallback; no assertion of a fire depends on them.\n\nconst SLOT_NAMES := [\"HitSpark0\", \"HitSpark1\", \"HitSpark2\", \"HitSpark3\"]\nconst LIFETIME_TICKS := 36               # hit_spark.tscn lifetime 0.6 s x 60 ticks/s\nconst HITSTOP := 4                       # main.gd HITSTOP_FRAMES\nconst HOLD_TICKS := 3                    # how long each key is held down\nconst POS_EPS := 1.0                     # rule 2: within 1 px in Main coordinates\nconst WALL_LIMIT_MS := 100000            # watchdog, under the wrapper's 120 s\n\nvar checks := 0\nvar failures := 0\nvar finished_run := false\nvar main: Node\nvar pool: Node\nvar slots: Array = []\nvar ticklog: TickLog\nvar sampler: Sampler\nvar setup_call: SetupCall\nvar results := []                        # attack_resolved of both fighters\nvar finished_log := []                   # {tick, slot}\nvar round_ticks := []                    # ticks on which round_started was emitted\nvar life_unpaused := -1                  # scenario B: hit tick -> emitting false, in ticks\n\n\n## Records every slot once per physics tick, after main (0), the pool (10) and SetupCall (50).\nclass TickLog extends Node:\n\tvar main: Node\n\tvar slots: Array = []\n\tvar recording := false\n\tvar ticks := {}\n\tvar order := []\n\tvar last_tick := -1\n\tvar prev: Array = []\n\tvar fires := []                      # {tick, slot, pos}\n\n\tfunc _ready() -> void:\n\t\tprocess_physics_priority = 1000\n\n\tfunc reset(m: Node, s: Array) -> void:\n\t\tmain = m\n\t\tslots = s\n\t\tticks.clear()\n\t\torder.clear()\n\t\tfires.clear()\n\t\tprev = []\n\t\tfor i in s.size():\n\t\t\tprev.append([false, Vector2.INF, 1.0])\n\n\tfunc _physics_process(_delta: float) -> void:\n\t\tif not (recording and is_instance_valid(main)):\n\t\t\treturn\n\t\tlast_tick = Engine.get_physics_frames()\n\t\tvar now := []\n\t\tfor i in slots.size():\n\t\t\tvar e: CPUParticles2D = slots[i]\n\t\t\tvar st := [e.emitting, e.position, e.speed_scale]\n\t\t\tif st[0] and (not prev[i][0] or st[1] != prev[i][1]):\n\t\t\t\tfires.append({\"tick\": last_tick, \"slot\": i, \"pos\": st[1]})\n\t\t\tnow.append(st)\n\t\tprev = now\n\t\tticks[last_tick] = {\"slots\": now, \"phase\": main.phase, \"paused\": main.paused,\n\t\t\t\t\"hitstop\": main.hitstop, \"p2\": main.p2.position}\n\t\torder.append(last_tick)\n\n\n## Records speed_scale once per rendered frame, after every other _process.\nclass Sampler extends Node:\n\tvar main: Node\n\tvar slots: Array = []\n\tvar recording := false\n\tvar frames := []                     # [process frame, paused, speeds]\n\tvar started_ms := 0\n\tvar on_watchdog: Callable\n\n\tfunc _ready() -> void:\n\t\tprocess_priority = 1000\n\t\tstarted_ms = Time.get_ticks_msec()\n\n\tfunc _process(_delta: float) -> void:\n\t\tif Time.get_ticks_msec() - started_ms > WALL_LIMIT_MS:\n\t\t\ton_watchdog.call()\n\t\tif recording and is_instance_valid(main):\n\t\t\tframes.append([Engine.get_process_frames(), main.paused,\n\t\t\t\t\tslots.map(func(e): return e.speed_scale)])\n\n\n## Runs one queued SETUP call inside a physics tick, after main and the pool, before TickLog.\nclass SetupCall extends Node:\n\tvar pending: Callable\n\tvar done_tick := -1\n\n\tfunc _ready() -> void:\n\t\tprocess_physics_priority = 50\n\n\tfunc _physics_process(_delta: float) -> void:\n\t\tif pending.is_valid():\n\t\t\tvar fn := pending\n\t\t\tpending = Callable()\n\t\t\tdone_tick = Engine.get_physics_frames()\n\t\t\tfn.call()\n\n\nfunc _initialize() -> void:\n\t_run.call_deferred()\n\n\nfunc _run() -> void:\n\tticklog = TickLog.new()\n\tsampler = Sampler.new()\n\tsampler.on_watchdog = _watchdog\n\tsetup_call = SetupCall.new()\n\troot.add_child(ticklog)\n\troot.add_child(sampler)\n\troot.add_child(setup_call)\n\tfor i in 10:\n\t\tawait process_frame\n\tprint(\"hit spark state test: Godot %s, %d physics ticks/s; headless dummy renderer, nothing is drawn\" % [\n\t\tEngine.get_version_info().string, ProjectSettings.get_setting(\"physics/common/physics_ticks_per_second\")])\n\tcheck(ClassDB.class_has_signal(\"CPUParticles2D\", \"finished\"), \"harness\",\n\t\t\t\"CPUParticles2D has a 'finished' signal in this build (the pool frees slots on it)\")\n\tawait scenario_load()\n\tawait scenario_single_hit()\n\tawait scenario_retrigger()\n\tawait scenario_free_fight()\n\tawait scenario_pause()\n\tawait scenario_round_reset_setup()\n\tfinish()\n\n\n# --- scenarios ---------------------------------------------------------------\n\nfunc scenario_load() -> void:\n\tif not await start_fight(\"A: scene load -> title -> Enter -> intro -> fight, no attack (rules 1, 3, 4)\", false, 30):\n\t\tawait end_fight()\n\t\treturn\n\tvar title_ticks: Array = ticklog.order.filter(func(x): return ticklog.ticks[x][\"phase\"] == \"title\")\n\tvar intro_ticks: Array = ticklog.order.filter(func(x): return ticklog.ticks[x][\"phase\"] == \"intro\")\n\tawait wait_ticks(30)\n\tvar any_on := ticklog.order.any(func(x): return ticklog.ticks[x][\"slots\"].any(func(s): return s[0]))\n\tcheck(ticklog.fires.is_empty() and not any_on and title_ticks.size() >= 30 and intro_ticks.size() >= 50, \"1\",\n\t\t\t\"no slot emitting on any of %d ticks from scene load (%d title, %d intro, then fight), %d fires\" % [\n\t\t\tticklog.order.size(), title_ticks.size(), intro_ticks.size(), ticklog.fires.size()])\n\tvar in_main := slots.size() == 4 and slots.all(func(e): return e is CPUParticles2D and e.get_parent() == main)\n\tvar total := 0\n\tfor e in slots:\n\t\ttotal += e.amount\n\tcheck(in_main and total == 80, \"3, 4\",\n\t\t\t\"4 CPUParticles2D slots, each a child of Main, %d particles in all (brief: 4 x 20 = 80)\" % total)\n\tvar under_fighters := 0\n\tfor f in [main.p1, main.p2]:\n\t\tunder_fighters += f.find_children(\"*\", \"CPUParticles2D\", true, false).size()\n\tcheck(under_fighters == 0, \"4\", \"no particle emitter under P1 or P2 (%d found)\" % under_fighters)\n\tawait end_fight()\n\n\nfunc scenario_single_hit() -> void:\n\tif not await start_fight(\"B: one punch on a standing Aotake (input only) (rules 1, 2, 4, 5)\", false):\n\t\tawait end_fight()\n\t\treturn\n\tif not await walk_into_punch_range():\n\t\tawait end_fight()\n\t\treturn\n\tawait tap(KEY_J, \"J (punch)\")\n\tawait wait_until(func(): return hits().size() >= 1, 30)\n\tvar h := hit(0)\n\tcheck(not h.is_empty(), \"harness\", \"P1's punch from the J key hit P2 (%s)\" % [result_names()])\n\tif h.is_empty():\n\t\tawait end_fight()\n\t\treturn\n\tawait wait_ticks(LIFETIME_TICKS + HITSTOP + 10)\n\tvar t: int = h[\"tick\"]\n\tvar f := fires_on(t)\n\tcheck(f.size() == 1 and ticklog.fires.size() == 1, \"1\",\n\t\t\t\"exactly one slot fired, on the hit tick T = %d (slot %s), and no fire on any other tick (%d in all)\" % [\n\t\t\tt, f.map(func(x): return x[\"slot\"]), ticklog.fires.size()])\n\tif f.size() != 1:\n\t\tawait end_fight()\n\t\treturn\n\tvar i: int = f[0][\"slot\"]\n\tvar e: CPUParticles2D = slots[i]\n\tcheck(e.position.distance_to(h[\"point\"]) <= POS_EPS and e.global_position.distance_to(main.to_global(h[\"point\"])) <= POS_EPS,\n\t\t\t\"2\", \"slot %d at %s, hit point %s (Main coordinates; global %s)\" % [i, e.position, h[\"point\"], e.global_position])\n\tvar fall := fall_after(i, t)\n\tvar moved: float = (tk(fall - 1).get(\"p2\", Vector2.ZERO) as Vector2).distance_to(tk(t).get(\"p2\", Vector2.ZERO))\n\tvar still := true\n\tfor x in range(t, fall):\n\t\tstill = still and tk(x)[\"slots\"][i][1] == h[\"point\"]\n\tcheck(fall > t and still and moved > 3.0, \"4\",\n\t\t\t\"the slot stayed at the hit point for its whole burst (T..T+%d) while P2 was pushed %.1f px\" % [fall - t - 1, moved])\n\tlife_unpaused = fall - t\n\tcheck(fall > t and life_unpaused >= LIFETIME_TICKS + HITSTOP - 1 and life_unpaused <= LIFETIME_TICKS + HITSTOP + 1, \"5\",\n\t\t\t\"emitting went false %d ticks after the hit: 36-tick lifetime + %d hitstop ticks held at speed_scale 0 (want 39-41)\" % [\n\t\t\tlife_unpaused, HITSTOP])\n\tprint(\"    'finished' after this burst on ticks %s (slot %d)\" % [finished_log.map(func(x): return x[\"tick\"] - t), i])\n\tawait end_fight()\n\n\nfunc scenario_retrigger() -> void:\n\tif not await start_fight(\"C: two punches inside one lifetime, Aotake cornered (input only) (rule 3)\", false):\n\t\tawait end_fight()\n\t\treturn\n\tsend_key(KEY_D, true)\n\tprint(\"    INPUT: D (walk right) held from after tick %d, pushing Aotake to the right wall\" % ticklog.last_tick)\n\tvar ok: bool = await wait_until(func(): return main.p2.position.x >= Fighter.ARENA_RIGHT - 0.01, 900)\n\tsend_key(KEY_D, false)\n\tvar idle: bool = await wait_until(func(): return main.p1.state == \"idle\", 30)\n\tcheck(ok and idle, \"harness\", \"Aotake at the right wall (x %.1f), P1 stopped at x %.1f\" % [main.p2.position.x, main.p1.position.x])\n\tawait tap(KEY_J, \"J (punch 1)\")\n\tawait wait_until(func(): return hits().size() >= 1, 30)\n\tawait wait_until(func(): return main.p1.state == \"idle\", 60)\n\tawait tap(KEY_J, \"J (punch 2)\")\n\tawait wait_until(func(): return hits().size() >= 2, 30)\n\tawait wait_ticks(LIFETIME_TICKS * 2 + 2 * HITSTOP + 10)\n\tcheck(hits().size() == 2, \"harness\", \"both punches hit (%s)\" % [result_names()])\n\tif hits().size() != 2:\n\t\tawait end_fight()\n\t\treturn\n\tvar t1: int = hit(0)[\"tick\"]\n\tvar t2: int = hit(1)[\"tick\"]\n\tvar f1 := fires_on(t1)\n\tvar f2 := fires_on(t2)\n\tcheck(t2 - t1 < LIFETIME_TICKS, \"harness\", \"second hit %d ticks after the first, inside one 36-tick lifetime\" % [t2 - t1])\n\tif f1.size() != 1 or f2.size() != 1:\n\t\tcheck(false, \"3\", \"one fire on each hit tick (got %d and %d)\" % [f1.size(), f2.size()])\n\t\tawait end_fight()\n\t\treturn\n\tvar a: int = f1[0][\"slot\"]\n\tvar b: int = f2[0][\"slot\"]\n\tprint(\"    hit 1 tick %d -> slot %d at %s; hit 2 tick %d -> slot %d at %s\" % [t1, a, f1[0][\"pos\"], t2, b, f2[0][\"pos\"]])\n\tcheck(a != b, \"3\", \"the second hit used another slot (%d, then %d), not the active one\" % [a, b])\n\tvar kept := true\n\tfor x in range(t1, t2 + 1):\n\t\tkept = kept and tk(x)[\"slots\"][a][0] and tk(x)[\"slots\"][a][1] == f1[0][\"pos\"]\n\tcheck(kept and tk(t2)[\"slots\"][b][0], \"3\",\n\t\t\t\"slot %d emitted on every tick T1..T2 at its own point, and on T2 both slots are emitting\" % a)\n\tvar fall_a := fall_after(a, t1)\n\tvar fall_b := fall_after(b, t2)\n\tcheck(fall_a > t2 and fall_a < t2 + LIFETIME_TICKS and fall_a < fall_b, \"3\",\n\t\t\t\"slot %d ran its own burst to the end: emitting false at T1+%d = T2+%d, before slot %d at T2+%d (a restart would end after T2+36)\" % [\n\t\t\ta, fall_a - t1, fall_a - t2, b, fall_b - t2])\n\tawait end_fight()\n\n\nfunc scenario_free_fight() -> void:\n\tif not await start_fight(\"D: a whole round against the game's CpuController, then Enter (rules 1, 2, 3, 6 real path)\", true):\n\t\tawait end_fight()\n\t\treturn\n\tawait tap(KEY_J, \"J (punch from across the arena, a whiff)\")\n\tawait wait_ticks(20)\n\tsend_key(KEY_L, true)\n\tprint(\"    INPUT: L (block) held from after tick %d\" % ticklog.last_tick)\n\tawait wait_ticks(200)\n\tsend_key(KEY_L, false)\n\tsend_key(KEY_D, true)\n\tprint(\"    INPUT: D held and J tapped every 24 ticks from after tick %d, until a K.O.\" % ticklog.last_tick)\n\tvar limit := Engine.get_physics_frames() + 4000\n\twhile main.phase == \"fight\" and Engine.get_physics_frames() < limit:\n\t\tsend_key(KEY_J, true)\n\t\tawait wait_ticks(HOLD_TICKS)\n\t\tsend_key(KEY_J, false)\n\t\tawait wait_ticks(21)\n\tsend_key(KEY_D, false)\n\tcheck(main.phase == \"ko\" or main.phase == \"result\", \"harness\", \"the round ended in a K.O. (phase %s)\" % main.phase)\n\tawait wait_until(func(): return main.phase == \"result\", 120)\n\tvar by := {}\n\tfor r in results:\n\t\tvar k := \"%s %s\" % [r[\"who\"], r[\"result\"]]\n\t\tby[k] = by.get(k, 0) + 1\n\tprint(\"    results: %s\" % [by])\n\tcheck(by.get(\"P1 hit\", 0) > 0 and by.get(\"P2 hit\", 0) > 0 and (by.get(\"P1 blocked\", 0) + by.get(\"P2 blocked\", 0)) > 0\n\t\t\tand (by.get(\"P1 whiff\", 0) + by.get(\"P2 whiff\", 0)) > 0, \"harness\",\n\t\t\t\"the round produced hits by both fighters, blocks and whiffs\")\n\tvar n_rounds := round_ticks.size()\n\tawait tap(KEY_ENTER, \"Enter (rematch on the result screen)\")\n\tawait wait_until(func(): return round_ticks.size() > n_rounds, 30)\n\tawait wait_ticks(40)\n\tif round_ticks.size() > n_rounds:\n\t\tvar rs: int = round_ticks[-1]\n\t\tvar off: bool = not tk(rs).get(\"slots\", [[true]]).any(func(s): return s[0])\n\t\tvar later: Array = ticklog.fires.filter(func(x): return x[\"tick\"] >= rs)\n\t\tvar last_fire: int = ticklog.fires[-1][\"tick\"] if not ticklog.fires.is_empty() else -1\n\t\tcheck(off and later.is_empty(), \"6\",\n\t\t\t\t\"real path: on the round_started tick (%d) no slot is emitting and none fires in the next 40 ticks (last burst fired %d ticks earlier, so this path cannot show a live burst being cleared)\" % [\n\t\t\t\trs, rs - last_fire])\n\telse:\n\t\tcheck(false, \"6\", \"Enter on the result screen started a new round\")\n\tawait end_fight()\n\n\nfunc scenario_pause() -> void:\n\tif not await start_fight(\"E: P pressed mid-burst for 40 ticks, then P again (input only) (rule 5)\", false):\n\t\tawait end_fight()\n\t\treturn\n\tif not await walk_into_punch_range():\n\t\tawait end_fight()\n\t\treturn\n\tawait tap(KEY_J, \"J (punch)\")\n\tawait wait_until(func(): return hits().size() >= 1, 30)\n\tawait wait_ticks(HITSTOP + 6)\n\tawait tap(KEY_P, \"P (pause)\")\n\tawait wait_ticks(40)\n\tawait tap(KEY_P, \"P (resume)\")\n\tawait wait_ticks(LIFETIME_TICKS + 10)\n\tvar h := hit(0)\n\tif h.is_empty() or fires_on(h[\"tick\"]).size() != 1:\n\t\tcheck(false, \"harness\", \"the punch hit and one slot fired (%s)\" % [result_names()])\n\t\tawait end_fight()\n\t\treturn\n\tvar t: int = h[\"tick\"]\n\tvar i: int = fires_on(t)[0][\"slot\"]\n\tvar paused: Array = ticklog.order.filter(func(x): return ticklog.ticks[x][\"paused\"])\n\tvar frozen := paused.all(func(x): return ticklog.ticks[x][\"slots\"].all(func(s): return s[2] == 0.0))\n\tvar pf: Array = sampler.frames.filter(func(s): return s[1])\n\tvar frozen_f := pf.all(func(s): return s[2].all(func(v): return v == 0.0))\n\tcheck(paused.size() >= 40 and frozen and pf.size() >= 40 and frozen_f, \"5\",\n\t\t\t\"speed_scale 0 on all 4 slots on all %d paused ticks and %d paused frames\" % [paused.size(), pf.size()])\n\tvar fall := fall_after(i, t)\n\tvar during: bool = paused.all(func(x): return x < fall and ticklog.ticks[x][\"slots\"][i][0])\n\tvar life := fall - t\n\tcheck(during and life_unpaused > 0 and absi(life - life_unpaused - paused.size()) <= 1, \"5\",\n\t\t\t\"the burst's clock stopped while paused: emitting false %d ticks after the hit = %d unpaused (scenario B) + %d paused\" % [\n\t\t\tlife, life_unpaused, paused.size()])\n\tawait end_fight()\n\n\nfunc scenario_round_reset_setup() -> void:\n\tif not await start_fight(\"F: SETUP main.start_fight_now() mid-burst, then a new punch (rule 6, Zhaohui's choice (b))\", false):\n\t\tawait end_fight()\n\t\treturn\n\tif not await walk_into_punch_range():\n\t\tawait end_fight()\n\t\treturn\n\tawait tap(KEY_J, \"J (punch 1)\")\n\tawait wait_until(func(): return hits().size() >= 1, 30)\n\tawait wait_ticks(HITSTOP + 6)\n\tvar h := hit(0)\n\tif h.is_empty() or fires_on(h[\"tick\"]).size() != 1:\n\t\tcheck(false, \"harness\", \"punch 1 hit and one slot fired (%s)\" % [result_names()])\n\t\tawait end_fight()\n\t\treturn\n\tvar i: int = fires_on(h[\"tick\"])[0][\"slot\"]\n\tcheck(tk(ticklog.last_tick)[\"slots\"][i][0], \"harness\", \"slot %d is mid-burst (hit tick +%d)\" % [i, ticklog.last_tick - h[\"tick\"]])\n\tvar fin_before := finished_log.size()\n\tsetup_call.done_tick = -1\n\tsetup_call.pending = func():\n\t\tprint(\"    SETUP (not input): main.start_fight_now() on tick T+%d, slot %d emitting\" % [\n\t\t\tEngine.get_physics_frames() - h[\"tick\"], i])\n\t\tmain.start_fight_now()\n\tawait wait_until(func(): return setup_call.done_tick >= 0, 10)\n\tvar s: int = setup_call.done_tick\n\tawait wait_ticks(LIFETIME_TICKS + 10)\n\tvar off: bool = not tk(s).get(\"slots\", [[true]]).any(func(x): return x[0])\n\tvar quiet: Array = ticklog.fires.filter(func(x): return x[\"tick\"] > h[\"tick\"])\n\tcheck(s >= 0 and off and quiet.is_empty(), \"6\",\n\t\t\t\"on the SETUP tick every slot stopped emitting (slot %d was mid-burst), and no slot fired in the next %d ticks\" % [\n\t\t\ti, LIFETIME_TICKS + 10])\n\tprint(\"    'finished' after the SETUP on ticks %s (slot: ticks after SETUP)\" % [\n\t\tfinished_log.slice(fin_before).map(func(x): return \"%d: %d\" % [x[\"slot\"], x[\"tick\"] - s])])\n\tif not await walk_into_punch_range():\n\t\tawait end_fight()\n\t\treturn\n\tawait tap(KEY_J, \"J (punch 2, in the new round)\")\n\tawait wait_until(func(): return hits().size() >= 2, 30)\n\tawait wait_ticks(5)\n\tvar h2 := hit(1)\n\tvar f2: Array = fires_on(h2[\"tick\"]) if not h2.is_empty() else []\n\tcheck(f2.size() == 1 and (f2[0][\"pos\"] as Vector2).distance_to(h2[\"point\"]) <= POS_EPS, \"6\",\n\t\t\t\"after the reset the next hit fires one slot (%s) at its point\" % [f2.map(func(x): return \"slot %d at %s\" % [x[\"slot\"], x[\"pos\"]])])\n\tawait end_fight()\n\n\n# --- checks over every scenario ---------------------------------------------\n\n## Rules 1 and 2 over the whole scene: on every tick, fires == \"hit\" results of both fighters, each\n## at its point; rule 3's fallback reported if it happened; rule 5 on every tick and frame.\nfunc check_scene() -> void:\n\tvar hit_by := {}\n\tfor r in results:\n\t\tif r[\"result\"] == \"hit\":\n\t\t\thit_by.get_or_add(r[\"tick\"], []).append(r)\n\tvar fire_by := {}\n\tfor f in ticklog.fires:\n\t\tfire_by.get_or_add(f[\"tick\"], []).append(f)\n\tvar bad := []\n\tvar fallback := 0\n\tfor t in hit_by:\n\t\tvar fs: Array = fire_by.get(t, []).duplicate()\n\t\tif fs.size() != hit_by[t].size():\n\t\t\tbad.append(\"tick %d: %d hits, %d fires\" % [t, hit_by[t].size(), fs.size()])\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\tfor r in hit_by[t]:\n\t\t\tvar j := -1\n\t\t\tfor k in fs.size():\n\t\t\t\tif (fs[k][\"pos\"] as Vector2).distance_to(r[\"point\"]) <= POS_EPS:\n\t\t\t\t\tj = k\n\t\t\tif j < 0:\n\t\t\t\tbad.append(\"tick %d: no fire at %s\" % [t, r[\"point\"]])\n\t\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t\tif not (r[\"busy\"] as Array).has(false):\n\t\t\t\tfallback += 1\n\t\t\t\tvar oldest: int = r[\"started\"].find(r[\"started\"].min())\n\t\t\t\tif fs[j][\"slot\"] != oldest:\n\t\t\t\t\tbad.append(\"tick %d: all busy, fired slot %d, oldest %d\" % [t, fs[j][\"slot\"], oldest])\n\t\t\tfs.remove_at(j)\n\tfor t in fire_by:\n\t\tif not hit_by.has(t):\n\t\t\tbad.append(\"tick %d: fire with no hit\" % t)\n\tvar other := results.filter(func(r): return r[\"result\"] != \"hit\").size()\n\tcheck(bad.is_empty(), \"1, 2\",\n\t\t\t\"scene: %d fires for %d hits, one per hit on its tick within 1 px of its point; none on %d other results or any other tick%s\" % [\n\t\t\tticklog.fires.size(), hit_by.values().reduce(func(n, a): return n + a.size(), 0), other,\n\t\t\t\"\" if bad.is_empty() else \": \" + \", \".join(bad.slice(0, 5))])\n\tprint(\"    rule 3 fallback (all four slots busy at a hit): %d time(s)%s\" % [fallback,\n\t\t\"\" if fallback else \"; not exercised in this scene\"])\n\tvar wrong := []\n\tfor t in ticklog.order:\n\t\tvar r: Dictionary = ticklog.ticks[t]\n\t\tvar want := 0.0 if (r[\"paused\"] or r[\"hitstop\"] > 0) else 1.0\n\t\tif not r[\"slots\"].all(func(s): return s[2] == want):\n\t\t\twrong.append(t)\n\tvar held: int = ticklog.order.filter(func(t): return ticklog.ticks[t][\"hitstop\"] > 0).size()\n\tcheck(wrong.is_empty(), \"5\",\n\t\t\t\"scene: speed_scale 0 on all 4 slots on every tick with main.paused or main.hitstop > 0 (%d hitstop ticks), 1 on the other %d ticks%s\" % [\n\t\t\theld, ticklog.order.size() - held, \"\" if wrong.is_empty() else \": wrong on ticks %s\" % [wrong.slice(0, 5)]])\n\n\n# --- helpers -----------------------------------------------------------------\n\nfunc start_fight(title: String, cpu: bool, title_ticks := 0) -> bool:\n\tprint(\"\\n== %s ==\" % title)\n\tmain = load(\"res://game/main.tscn\").instantiate()\n\tpool = main.get_node(\"HitSparkPool\")\n\tslots = SLOT_NAMES.map(func(n): return main.get_node(n))\n\tresults.clear()\n\tfinished_log.clear()\n\tround_ticks.clear()\n\tsampler.frames.clear()\n\tticklog.reset(main, slots)\n\tsampler.main = main\n\tsampler.slots = slots\n\t# Connected before main enters the tree, so these run before the pool's handler (snapshot of\n\t# the pool's busy state for the fallback report) and before main's.\n\tfor f in [main.get_node(\"P1\"), main.get_node(\"P2\")]:\n\t\tf.attack_resolved.connect(func(_f, kind, result, point):\n\t\t\tresults.append({\"tick\": Engine.get_physics_frames(), \"who\": \"P1\" if f.name == \"P1\" else \"P2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"kind\": kind, \"result\": result, \"point\": point,\n\t\t\t\t\"busy\": pool.busy.duplicate(), \"started\": pool.started.duplicate()}))\n\tfor i in slots.size():\n\t\tslots[i].finished.connect(func(): finished_log.append({\"tick\": Engine.get_physics_frames(), \"slot\": i}))\n\tmain.round_started.connect(func(_n): round_ticks.append(Engine.get_physics_frames()))\n\tif not cpu:\n\t\tmain.round_started.connect(func(_n): main.p2.controller = null)\n\tticklog.recording = true\n\tsampler.recording = true\n\troot.add_child(main)\n\tawait process_frame\n\tcheck(main.is_physics_processing() and main.p1.controller is PlayerController, \"harness\",\n\t\t\t\"main's _physics_process is on and P1 is driven by its PlayerController\")\n\tawait wait_ticks(title_ticks)\n\tawait tap(KEY_ENTER, \"Enter (title)\")\n\tvar ok := await wait_until(func(): return main.phase == \"fight\", 120)\n\tcheck(ok, \"harness\", \"Enter on the title started round 1; the intro ran into the fight (phase %s)\" % main.phase)\n\tif not cpu:\n\t\tprint(\"    HARNESS (writes no fight state): P2's controller set to null when the round starts, so Aotake stands still\")\n\treturn ok\n\n\nfunc end_fight() -> void:\n\tfor k in [KEY_D, KEY_J, KEY_L, KEY_P, KEY_ENTER]:\n\t\tsend_key(k, false)\n\tsetup_call.pending = Callable()\n\tticklog.recording = false\n\tsampler.recording = false\n\tif is_instance_valid(main):\n\t\tcheck_scene()\n\t\tvar kept := slots.duplicate()\n\t\tmain.queue_free()\n\t\tawait process_frame\n\t\tawait process_frame\n\t\tcheck(kept.all(func(e): return not is_instance_valid(e)), \"4\",\n\t\t\t\t\"freeing Main freed all 4 slots with it\")\n\n\nfunc walk_into_punch_range() -> bool:\n\tvar gap: float = main.p1.reach(\"punch\") + main.p2.body_half_width() - 8.0\n\tsend_key(KEY_D, true)\n\tprint(\"    INPUT: D (walk right) held from after tick %d\" % ticklog.last_tick)\n\tvar ok: bool = await wait_until(func(): return main.p2.position.x - main.p1.position.x <= gap, 300)\n\tsend_key(KEY_D, false)\n\tvar idle: bool = await wait_until(func(): return main.p1.state == \"idle\", 30)\n\tcheck(ok and idle, \"harness\", \"P1 walked to punch range with the D key (gap %.1f px, target <= %.1f) and stopped\" % [\n\t\tmain.p2.position.x - main.p1.position.x, gap])\n\treturn ok and idle\n\n\nfunc hits() -> Array:\n\treturn results.filter(func(r): return r[\"result\"] == \"hit\")\n\n\nfunc hit(index: int) -> Dictionary:\n\tvar h := hits()\n\treturn h[index] if h.size() > index else {}\n\n\nfunc result_names() -> Array:\n\treturn results.map(func(r): return \"%s %s %s\" % [r[\"who\"], r[\"kind\"], r[\"result\"]])\n\n\nfunc fires_on(t: int) -> Array:\n\treturn ticklog.fires.filter(func(f): return f[\"tick\"] == t)\n\n\n## First recorded tick after t0 on which slot i is not emitting, or -1.\nfunc fall_after(i: int, t0: int) -> int:\n\tfor t in ticklog.order:\n\t\tif t > t0 and not ticklog.ticks[t][\"slots\"][i][0]:\n\t\t\treturn t\n\treturn -1\n\n\nfunc tk(t: int) -> Dictionary:\n\treturn ticklog.ticks.get(t, {})\n\n\nfunc send_key(code: Key, pressed: bool) -> void:\n\tvar ev := InputEventKey.new()\n\tev.keycode = code\n\tev.physical_keycode = code\n\tev.pressed = pressed\n\tInput.parse_input_event(ev)\n\n\nfunc tap(code: Key, label: String) -> void:\n\tsend_key(code, true)\n\tprint(\"    INPUT: %s pressed after tick %d\" % [label, ticklog.last_tick])\n\tawait wait_ticks(HOLD_TICKS)\n\tsend_key(code, false)\n\tawait process_frame\n\n\nfunc wait_until(cond: Callable, max_ticks: int) -> bool:\n\tvar limit := Engine.get_physics_frames() + max_ticks\n\twhile not cond.call():\n\t\tif Engine.get_physics_frames() > limit:\n\t\t\treturn false\n\t\tawait process_frame\n\treturn true\n\n\nfunc wait_ticks(n: int) -> void:\n\tvar limit := Engine.get_physics_frames() + n\n\twhile Engine.get_physics_frames() < limit:\n\t\tawait process_frame\n\n\nfunc check(cond: bool, rule: String, msg: String) -> void:\n\tchecks += 1\n\tif not cond:\n\t\tfailures += 1\n\tprint(\"%s [%s] %s\" % [\"PASS\" if cond else \"FAIL\", rule, msg])\n\n\nfunc _watchdog() -> void:\n\tif finished_run:\n\t\treturn\n\tcheck(false, \"harness\", \"watchdog: not finished after %d s of wall-clock time\" % (WALL_LIMIT_MS / 1000))\n\tfinish()\n\n\nfunc finish() -> void:\n\tif finished_run:\n\t\treturn\n\tfinished_run = true\n\tprint(\"%d checks, %d failed\" % [checks, failures])\n\tquit(1 if failures else 0)\n","numLines":592,"startLine":1,"totalLines":592}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016QNJHmVRkNSRF8d6Lahkbi","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
