{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017VAgR66rZC8K2dwFbz4nVr","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tRead CLAUDE.md first. CHANGE-BRIEF.md is the contract for this change.\n2\tEffect B's scene is built and its configuration test passes. Do not\n3\tchange the effect's settings in this task, and do not edit any\n4\t.gdshader file.\n5\t\n6\tFirst propose the smallest plan that meets the brief: the code that\n7\tstarts and stops Effect B on its condition, and a new state test in\n8\tgodot/tests/. Say which brief rule each assertion covers, and which\n9\trules only a human can check. Do not edit yet.\n10\t\n11\tAfter I approve a step, implement only that step and show the diff.\n12\tRules:\n13\t- Presentation code may read game state; it never writes it. Do not\n14\t  change collision, movement, input, the state machine or the existing\n15\t  tests.\n16\t- The test drives the condition through the real game loop and real\n17\t  input, never by calling the start or stop function directly.\n18\t- It asserts that the effect starts when the condition begins and\n19\t  stops when it ends, and what it does while the tree is paused and\n20\t  while the node is hidden, as the brief says.\n21\t- For a feedback loop, it sets the game value to at least two values\n22\t  and asserts that the code changes amount_ratio, not amount.\n23\t- Run every test with ./scripts/run-test.sh: the existing ones as\n24\t  CLAUDE.md says, and the new one at 60, or in realtime if it waits on\n25\t  audio. Show the real output and say which mode you used.\n26\t- Say exactly what the test proves and what it cannot prove headlessly.\n27\t- Do not commit.\n28\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"448404b5-eb92-49c5-9cad-ea968beeb155","uuid":"58d2a741-066d-4909-9653-197cd69d17ab","timestamp":"2026-11-08T21:49:39.940Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"D:\\courses\\7270\\walker-dusk-duel-zhaohui-li\\prompts\\a6\\prompt-6-plan-embers.txt","content"